  /** Starts a conversation, or continues one when `after` names a turn.
The run is accepted, not finished: follow it on the event stream at
topic `agent:<agent>:<id>`, or poll `getRun`.

Send `Idempotency-Key` to make a retry safe. The run's `tag_id` is
then `api-<length of subject in bytes>-<subject>-<key>`, its `id` is
derived from that and the workspace (`r` and 32 hex digits, as
fiber's `runtime.RunID`), and a second request with the same key
from the same caller joins the run the first one started instead of
starting another. Without it the ids are random.

A conversation filed in a project that was deleted since is read,
not continued: its next turn answers 409, since nothing says any more
which projects above it the run would count toward.

The body takes no metadata: an unknown field answers 400.

Nothing routes on its own. With `agent` left out, the default the
conversation's place inherits answers, the first set of: the
thread's (`updateThread`), the acting client's when `act_as` names
one, the channel's (a new conversation is in `general` of its
project), then the project's, each ancestor's nearest first, and the
workspace's. With none set it is 409, "tag an agent". `auto` is
`@auto`, which for a person a client acts for picks only among the
agents that client may route to. An agent not available in the
conversation's project, or a default that has stopped being
available there, is 403. So is a conversation in a project where the
caller, or the person `act_as` names, is only a viewer: starting work
in a project, or adding a turn to work filed there, needs a member.
The person `act_as` names must hold `runs:write` themselves, as for
posting and answering for them, or it is 403: the credential's own is
not enough.

A follow-up is filed in its conversation's channel. When it follows
a turn in a shared thread people have posted in, it is sent the room
up to that turn, one turn a line after who took it: people's
messages and earlier follow-ups by the name and handle of who wrote
or asked them, or as acting for nobody, and agents' answers by
theirs. The room is fenced off from the follow-up's own words, which
follow with who asks them, and the follow-up is part of the room the
agents answering the next message are sent.
 */
  async createRun(body: CreateRunRequest, idempotencyKey?: string, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<Run> {
    const path = "/api/runs";
    const _hdr: Record<string, string> = {};
    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries({ "Idempotency-Key": idempotencyKey })) {
      if (v !== undefined && v !== null) _hdr[k] = String(v);
    }
    return this.request<Run>("POST", path, {
      body,
      contentType: "application/json",
      signal: options?.signal,
      headers: { ..._hdr, ...options?.headers },
      retry: options?.retry,
      timeout: options?.timeout,
    });
  }

